  "format": "tribrach.conformance.wire.v1",
  "about": "How each wire primitive reads and writes JSON (Tribrach.Wire). Each case has a JSON Schema as core exports it, an input as JSON text, and either output, the JSON the codec writes after reading the input, or error: true when reading fails. Instruments parse the input with their own JSON parser, read it as the schema says, write it back and compare with output by the JSON equality of replay.json. Reading fails on text that isn't one JSON value (trailing data, a trailing comma, NaN) and on an object with a duplicated key. Whole numbers may be written 2.0 or 1e2 and are written back plainly; instants are written back in UTC, and an instant whose day doesn't exist in its month (30 February, 29 February outside leap years) fails. Cases stay within signed 64-bit integers.",
